    "narrative": "Our core strategy today hinges on capitalizing on high-ceiling matchups against manageable arms, led by **Brice Turang** (73.37) and **Corbin Carroll** (72.42). **Brice Turang** is our strongest play; he benefits from a significant +14% park boost and, crucially, a +4% efficiency jump due to the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which massively inflates his stolen base probability\u2014the lifeblood of our Roto aspirations. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** is locked into the two-hole with a strong +6% platoon edge, making him a prime candidate to anchor our R and SB production against Cavalli. Rounding out the top tier, **Josh Naylor** (67.78) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (66.19) provide reliable power, with **Josh Naylor** capitalizing on an favorable park factor and a favorable slot in the order to drive in runs.\n\nThe most challenging decision on the bench involved **Alex Freeland**, who posted a 43.86, hovering just below our threshold for starting consideration. While **Alex Freeland** offers switch-hitting versatility, his placement at the bottom of the order (-8% penalty) ultimately relegated him to the bench behind the steadier output of **Zach McKinstry** and **Cole Young**, who both benefit from higher lineup placement and specific park-driven advantages. We are also keeping a wary eye on **Seiya Suzuki** (44.34); his score is suppressed heavily by a -19% SP skill penalty, reflecting the difficulty of facing McDonald. We remain cautious with **Vinnie Pasquantino** (50.31) as well, given the aggressive -15% platoon penalty against Prielipp, though his base projection remains high enough to merit a spot in the utility slot over the deeper bench options like **Austin Riley** or **Travis Bazzana**, both of whom are facing elite arms that severely cap their daily ceilings.",
